      explanation: "<b>Step 1:</b> The two flight segments form two sides of a triangle, with lengths 180 meters and 420 meters.<br><br><b>Step 2:</b> Since the second segment is 35° west of north, the angle between the two traveled segments is 35°.<br><br><b>Step 3:</b> For the triangle whose third side is the direct distance from start to finish, the included interior angle between the two sides drawn tail-to-tail corresponds to 180° − 35° = 145°.<br><br><b>Step 4:</b> Apply the Law of Cosines:<br>d² = 180² + 420² − 2(180)(420)cos 145°.<br><br><b>Step 5:</b> Since cos 145° = −cos 35°, this is equivalent to:<br>d = √(180² + 420² + 2(180)(420)cos 35°).<br><br><b>Answer:</b> <b>√(180² + 420² + 2(180)(420)cos 35°)</b>.",
