      explanation: "<b>Step 1:</b> The introductory phrase “After surveying the cliffs for a workable route” must describe the subject that immediately follows it.<br><br><b>Step 2:</b> The engineers performed the surveying, so “the engineers” must follow the introductory phrase. The original sentence illogically suggests that the terrain surveyed the cliffs, while the other choices attach the action to the cliffs or to “a direct ascent.”<br><br><b>Answer:</b> “After surveying the cliffs for a workable route, the engineers abandoned a direct ascent” creates a clear and logical modifier relationship.",
      practiceYear: 4,
