      correctAnswer: "The artistic effects of technology depend partly on how people adapt to its limitations and the conditions under which it is used.",
      explanation: "<b>Step 1:</b> The passage repeatedly separates technical capability from practical adoption: costs, electrical infrastructure, trained crews, and standardization affect when equipment can actually shape productions.<br><br><b>Step 2:</b> Other examples show that people actively transform constraints into practices—the touring troupe turns scarce lanterns into a compositional method, and the separation of designer and operator encourages numbered lighting cues.<br><br><b>Step 3:</b> Combining those ideas shows that the author regards technology as influential but not independently determining; its artistic effects emerge through adaptation, access, inherited habits, and workplace conditions.<br><br><b>Answer:</b> The artistic effects of technology depend partly on how people adapt to its limitations and the conditions under which it is used.",
